{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Cuts resonances as they happen, and makes room for another track by dipping the frequencies that track is using.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Resonances: raise Depth for stronger cuts, lower Threshold to catch smaller peaks, and set Sharpness for broad smoothing (low) or narrow peaks (high). Listen set to Removed plays only what the plugin takes out.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Making room: send the other track to channels 3 and 4 of this track, which needs 4 channels. For ducking only, set Depth to 0.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Ducks a track on every hit of a sidechain, of the track itself or of MIDI notes. A volume curve shapes each duck, a second curve can duck the low band on its own, and Follow ring-modulates the track with the sidechain.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Sidechain: send the kick to channels 3 and 4 of this track, which needs 4 channels. Set Trigger to Main input to duck on the track's own hits, or to MIDI notes to duck on every note-on.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Learned curve: set Curve mode to Learn and play a few bars of the kick. Nothing is ducked while it learns. Then set Curve mode to Match: both curves follow the kick until it has faded. Volume scale and Sub scale change each curve's length.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Plays a reverse reverb swell before every item on its track. The swell rises into the item's first sound and fades out just after it, in sync with the project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Select the track that holds the items and run Track: Prevent track media buffering. Without it, swells in the first seconds after you press Play stay silent.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab At 100 % Dry/wet, the default, only the swells play: put it on a copy of the items' track or on a send.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Each item needs at least 5 ms of silence before it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Pre-echoes, a tempo-synced tremolo and a filter sweep can build into each item.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The latency is as long as the swell, up to 5.3 s at 48 kHz, so don't monitor live input through it.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Delays each frequency by its own amount, so a click comes out as a chirp: laser-like allpass smears, sweeps, rising or falling echoes and scattered textures.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Classic: a chain of allpass filters with no latency. Disperse stages sets the length of the chirp, Disperse frequency where it centres, and Disperse Q how narrow it rings.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Spectral: adds a delay for each octave band, Scatter, Stereo spread, note tuning with harmonics, and Feedback with Shift per echo. Its latency of one FFT is compensated by REAPER.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Real-time pitch correction for vocals and monophonic instruments.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Corrects to the nearest note of a key and scale, or to the notes held on its MIDI input. Each note can follow the scale, be added, removed or bypassed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Retune speed sets how fast a note reaches its target, Humanize slows the correction of sustained notes, and Flex-tune corrects only notes sung close to their target.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Natural vibrato scales the singer's vibrato; Vibrato depth, rate and delay add one.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Formants are kept when shifting (Preserve formants) and can be shifted on their own.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Latency depends on Input type (6 to 25 ms at 48 kHz) and is compensated by REAPER.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A lush, modulated reverb that goes from a tight room to endless soundscapes, with Freeze to hold the tail.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The granular section, off by default, plays grains from the reverb tail or the input: pitched, reversed and scattered across the stereo field, and fed back into the reverb if you want clouds that build on themselves.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Slows a track down like a stopping tape or turntable. Automate Playrate and the envelope is the stop curve. A long sinc interpolator keeps the highs clean as the pitch drops.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Tape stop: ramp Playrate from 100 % down to 0 %, then jump back to 100 % where the music returns.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Tape start: jump to 0 % and ramp up to 100 %.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Resync at 100%: On crossfades back in time with the track when Playrate reaches 100 %. Off keeps the lag.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Blind Producers ReaPack repository\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER plugins from Blind Producers, installed and updated through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab In REAPER, choose Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Paste this URL and press OK:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/BlindProducers/reapack/raw/main/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Choose Extensions > ReaPack > Browse packages and install the plugins you want.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Update\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Choose Extensions > ReaPack > Synchronize packages. ReaPack updates every installed plugin to its latest version.\par}
}
